 "note": "RPCS3 Core 929 = Core 928 with the restored memory of a savestate left as saved (REWINDBOX_GOW3_MLAA_SAVESTATE_UNTOUCHED_929). Core 922 wrote the God of War III MLAA bypass pair into the restored memory of a savestate made without it; the game resumed with its MLAA set up and its own flag cleared, and the picture broke at the first pause menu on resumed sessions of builds 724 and 725 (maintainer, 11 Nov). The pair is written at a fresh boot only, as upstream applies every executable patch; a savestate made after a fresh boot holds it. Core 928 (pinned d45b1c80, run 42960159566: the GPU gate closed at the deactivation, asynchronous MoltenVK submits for every title, texture lookup memo for Black Ops II, GPU memory packing, the deferral to a starving PPU before the line lock), unchanged otherwise. No codegen input changes: PPU and SPU codegen identities unchanged. MoltenVK dependency of run 42998604606 (libMoltenVK.a d19d3a42, the same library). Host bridge of this source: the in-game menu shows the applied resolution (compiled with the iPhone SDK by run 42994454001). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 43000618405, attempt 1, source 1ea6cf4a; Apple host harnesses run 43000618405 on 1ea6cf4a). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle); the packaged library no longer holds the Core 922 savestate message. Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
